1
00:00:02,509 --> 00:00:03,551
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,969 --> 00:00:06,012
Earth.

3
00:00:06,846 --> 00:00:07,889
Fire.

4
00:00:08,973 --> 00:00:10,016
Air.

5
00:00:11,184 --> 00:00:15,146
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,396 --> 00:00:18,775
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,651 --> 00:00:22,487
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:23,780
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,863 --> 00:00:26,699
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

10
00:00:27,325 --> 00:00:29,786
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

11
00:00:29,869 --> 00:00:32,872
the new Avatar, an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:32,956 --> 00:00:35,166
And although
his airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:37,502
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,627 --> 00:00:38,836
AANG: Oof!

15
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:42,090
But I believe Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:42,465 --> 00:00:44,467
♪

17
00:00:47,949 --> 00:00:49,951
♪

18
00:00:56,457 --> 00:00:59,377
( BOILING )

19
00:01:02,213 --> 00:01:03,881
Line 'em up for the warden!

20
00:01:03,965 --> 00:01:07,260
♪

21
00:01:12,682 --> 00:01:13,891
Dad.

22
00:01:15,268 --> 00:01:16,727
Excuse me, coming through!

23
00:01:16,811 --> 00:01:18,563
The warden wants me over there, sorry!

24
00:01:20,815 --> 00:01:23,401
WARDEN: Welcome to the Boiling Rock.

25
00:01:23,484 --> 00:01:25,736
I'm sure you've all heard
the horrible rumors

26
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:27,780
about our little island.

27
00:01:27,864 --> 00:01:31,451
Well, I just want to tell you
that they don't have to be true,

28
00:01:31,534 --> 00:01:34,620
as long as you do everything I say.

29
00:01:35,288 --> 00:01:37,748
Look me in the eye
when I'm talking to you.

30
00:01:38,249 --> 00:01:39,459
No.

31
00:01:39,542 --> 00:01:42,879
Oh, you'd rather look at my shoes?

32
00:01:43,004 --> 00:01:44,422
Then take a look!

33
00:01:44,881 --> 00:01:46,174
Aah!

34
00:01:47,508 --> 00:01:51,429
I know exactly who you are,
Hakoda of the Water Tribe.

35
00:01:51,512 --> 00:01:53,431
So strong-willed.

36
00:01:53,514 --> 00:01:57,059
But don't worry.
We'll get rid of that in time.

37
00:01:57,143 --> 00:01:58,978
Now look me in the eye!

38
00:01:59,061 --> 00:02:00,980
( WATER BOILING )

39
00:02:03,024 --> 00:02:05,151
See, isn't that better?

40
00:02:05,234 --> 00:02:08,321
You will all do as I say or pay the price.

41
00:02:08,404 --> 00:02:10,198
You will always... ( GRUNTS )

42
00:02:10,281 --> 00:02:11,491
( SPUTTERS )

43
00:02:12,825 --> 00:02:15,536
- Are you okay, sir?
- I'm fine!

44
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:18,080
Get these prisoners out of my sight.

45
00:02:18,164 --> 00:02:20,917
♪

46
00:02:29,884 --> 00:02:30,968
( DOOR OPENS )

47
00:02:33,387 --> 00:02:35,223
Thank goodness you're okay!

48
00:02:35,348 --> 00:02:40,436
If you take one step closer,
you'll see just how okay I am.

49
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,938
Dad, it's me.

50
00:02:43,272 --> 00:02:44,482
Sokka?

51
00:02:45,149 --> 00:02:46,567
My son.

52
00:02:47,735 --> 00:02:49,654
( CHUCKLES ) You know, Sokka,

53
00:02:49,779 --> 00:02:52,281
you should be more careful
with that guard outfit on.

54
00:02:52,365 --> 00:02:53,991
I almost punched you in the gut.

55
00:02:54,075 --> 00:02:56,619
Yeah, I ran into that problem earlier.

56
00:02:56,702 --> 00:02:59,622
( FOOTSTEPS )

57
00:03:00,331 --> 00:03:01,541
( CLANK )

58
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,211
Are you comfortable, Chit Sang?

59
00:03:05,294 --> 00:03:07,880
If you're trying to get me
to talk, forget it!

60
00:03:07,964 --> 00:03:09,340
I'm not a squealer.

61
00:03:10,675 --> 00:03:13,553
Chit Sang, I only ask you
if you were comfortable.

62
00:03:13,636 --> 00:03:16,847
Well, yeah, actually,
I am pretty comfortable.

63
00:03:17,723 --> 00:03:18,891
( GRUNTS )

64
00:03:20,476 --> 00:03:22,061
WARDEN: Are you still comfortable?

65
00:03:22,144 --> 00:03:23,187
No.

66
00:03:23,271 --> 00:03:25,690
WARDEN: I know you and your cronies
are not smart enough

67
00:03:25,773 --> 00:03:28,276
to come up with that little escape plan.

68
00:03:28,359 --> 00:03:31,445
So you're gonna tell me who is.

69
00:03:31,529 --> 00:03:33,531
( TENSE MUSIC )

70
00:03:36,033 --> 00:03:38,035
♪

71
00:03:44,584 --> 00:03:46,210
SOKKA: So where's Bato?

72
00:03:46,294 --> 00:03:48,129
Where's everyone else from the invasion?

73
00:03:48,212 --> 00:03:49,547
The others are being held

74
00:03:49,630 --> 00:03:51,507
at a prison near the Fire Nation palace.

75
00:03:51,591 --> 00:03:54,135
They singled me out as their leader
and sent me here.

76
00:03:54,385 --> 00:03:55,845
But before I left,

77
00:03:55,928 --> 00:03:58,389
I met some young women
who said they knew you.

78
00:03:58,472 --> 00:04:00,558
The Oshinama Fighters?

79
00:04:00,641 --> 00:04:03,561
- You mean the Kyoshi Warriors?
- That's right.

80
00:04:03,644 --> 00:04:06,772
Their leader, Suki, is here,
and she's gonna escape with us.

81
00:04:06,856 --> 00:04:09,066
Good, we'll need all the help we can get.

82
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:12,320
- And you know Prince Zuko?
- The son of the Fire Lord?

83
00:04:12,403 --> 00:04:14,739
I don't know him, but I know of him.

84
00:04:14,822 --> 00:04:18,284
- Well, he's here, too.
- Sounds like a major problem.

85
00:04:18,367 --> 00:04:20,494
Actually, he's on our side now.

86
00:04:22,371 --> 00:04:24,373
I know, I had the same reaction.

87
00:04:24,457 --> 00:04:26,667
After all he's done,
it was hard to trust him.

88
00:04:26,751 --> 00:04:28,252
But he's really proven himself,

89
00:04:28,336 --> 00:04:30,588
and I never would've found you
without his help.

90
00:04:31,672 --> 00:04:34,133
So, do you have a plan?

91
00:04:34,216 --> 00:04:35,509
We had one,

92
00:04:35,593 --> 00:04:38,179
but some of the other prisoners
got involved and ruined it.

93
00:04:38,262 --> 00:04:40,806
I don't know if there's
another way off this island.

94
00:04:40,890 --> 00:04:43,351
Sokka, there's no prison in the world

95
00:04:43,434 --> 00:04:45,603
that can hold two Water Tribe geniuses.

96
00:04:45,728 --> 00:04:47,855
Then we better find two.

97
00:04:48,564 --> 00:04:50,566
( LAUGHS )

98
00:04:50,650 --> 00:04:52,610
( CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY )

99
00:04:53,778 --> 00:04:55,780
( TENSE MUSIC )

100
00:04:58,032 --> 00:05:00,034
♪

101
00:05:02,036 --> 00:05:03,871
Zuko, are you there?

102
00:05:03,954 --> 00:05:05,373
I'm here.

103
00:05:05,456 --> 00:05:07,333
I just got done talking to my dad.

104
00:05:07,416 --> 00:05:09,293
We came up with an escape plan together.

105
00:05:09,377 --> 00:05:11,128
MALE GUARD: What are you doing here?

106
00:05:12,713 --> 00:05:15,800
I was just telling this dirty
lowlife what I think of him!

107
00:05:15,883 --> 00:05:17,677
Well, you'll have to do that later.

108
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:18,969
He's coming with us.

109
00:05:19,053 --> 00:05:20,596
Why?

110
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:22,640
Because we have orders
straight from the warden,

111
00:05:22,723 --> 00:05:23,891
that's why.

112
00:05:23,974 --> 00:05:26,811
Could I just get 10 more seconds
to rough him up a bit?

113
00:05:27,770 --> 00:05:29,397
Fine, 10 seconds.

114
00:05:30,064 --> 00:05:31,982
( OPENS AND SHUTS DOOR )

115
00:05:32,066 --> 00:05:34,402
SOKKA: Take that! And this!

116
00:05:34,485 --> 00:05:35,528
Newbie!

117
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:38,280
( ZUKO GRUNTING )

118
00:05:40,032 --> 00:05:42,576
We have a new plan, but it's
gonna need a big distraction.

119
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:44,787
- Be in the yard in one hour.
-( DOOR OPENS )

120
00:05:46,288 --> 00:05:47,415
( GROANING )

121
00:05:47,498 --> 00:05:49,667
All right, that's enough.

122
00:05:52,086 --> 00:05:55,005
ZUKO: What are you doing?
Where are you taking me?

123
00:05:56,590 --> 00:06:00,469
Aah! I didn't do anything wrong.

124
00:06:00,594 --> 00:06:03,764
Come on, Zuko. We all know that's a lie.

125
00:06:03,848 --> 00:06:04,974
Mai.

126
00:06:07,059 --> 00:06:09,061
( FOOTSTEPS )

127
00:06:11,814 --> 00:06:15,276
- How is he?
- I think he's ready to talk.

128
00:06:15,359 --> 00:06:17,153
( GROANS )

129
00:06:17,236 --> 00:06:20,531
( PANTS )

130
00:06:20,614 --> 00:06:24,285
Have you had enough time
to think about what I asked?

131
00:06:24,535 --> 00:06:26,454
- Yes.
- And?

132
00:06:26,537 --> 00:06:28,205
You're right.

133
00:06:28,289 --> 00:06:31,041
There was another person
involved in the escape plan.

134
00:06:31,125 --> 00:06:32,168
Who?

135
00:06:32,251 --> 00:06:34,545
It's a guy who's disguised
like a prison guard,

136
00:06:34,628 --> 00:06:36,422
only he's not a prison guard.

137
00:06:36,505 --> 00:06:39,717
He's the mastermind.
He came up with the plan.

138
00:06:53,898 --> 00:06:57,693
- How did you know I was here?
- Because I know you so well.

139
00:06:57,777 --> 00:06:59,069
But how...

140
00:06:59,153 --> 00:07:01,155
The warden's my uncle, you idiot.

141
00:07:01,530 --> 00:07:02,823
( GROANS )

142
00:07:02,907 --> 00:07:06,160
The truth is, I guess I don't know you.

143
00:07:06,243 --> 00:07:07,703
All I get is a letter?

144
00:07:07,828 --> 00:07:09,538
You could've at least looked me in the eye

145
00:07:09,622 --> 00:07:11,165
when you ripped out my heart.

146
00:07:11,749 --> 00:07:14,251
- I didn't mean to...
- You didn't mean to?

147
00:07:15,085 --> 00:07:18,714
"Dear Mai, I'm sorry that
you have to find out this way,

148
00:07:18,798 --> 00:07:20,132
"but I'm leaving."

149
00:07:20,216 --> 00:07:22,259
Stop! This isn't about you!

150
00:07:22,343 --> 00:07:24,220
This is about the Fire Nation.

151
00:07:24,303 --> 00:07:27,723
Thanks, Zuko.
That makes me feel all better.

152
00:07:29,225 --> 00:07:31,769
Mai, I never wanted to hurt you.

153
00:07:32,186 --> 00:07:34,730
But I have to do this to save my country.

154
00:07:34,814 --> 00:07:37,650
Save it? You're betraying your country.

155
00:07:37,733 --> 00:07:39,360
That's not how I see it.

156
00:07:41,779 --> 00:07:43,781
( WHOOSHING )

157
00:07:49,036 --> 00:07:52,289
- Sokka, what's going on?
- I don't have much time.

158
00:07:52,373 --> 00:07:55,084
If I'm seen with you, the guards
might think something's up.

159
00:07:56,585 --> 00:07:59,421
- I just talked to my dad.
- That's great.

160
00:07:59,505 --> 00:08:02,800
Yeah, and we're escaping
today... on the gondola.

161
00:08:02,883 --> 00:08:03,926
What?

162
00:08:04,009 --> 00:08:06,136
My dad and I came up
with the plan together.

163
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:07,596
We're gonna commandeer the gondola

164
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,181
and we're gonna take a hostage with us

165
00:08:09,265 --> 00:08:10,641
so they won't cut the lines.

166
00:08:10,724 --> 00:08:12,852
We'll never make it on to the gondola.

167
00:08:12,935 --> 00:08:14,603
There's too many guards.

168
00:08:14,687 --> 00:08:16,272
My dad already thought of that.

169
00:08:16,355 --> 00:08:18,065
He said we'll need a distraction.

170
00:08:18,148 --> 00:08:20,317
That's why we're gonna
start a prison riot.

171
00:08:21,527 --> 00:08:24,405
Okay, let's say by some
miracle this all works

172
00:08:24,488 --> 00:08:25,865
and we make it on the gondola.

173
00:08:25,948 --> 00:08:27,825
The warden will still just cut the lines

174
00:08:27,908 --> 00:08:29,493
even if we have a captive.

175
00:08:29,577 --> 00:08:32,162
Not if the warden is the captive.

176
00:08:32,454 --> 00:08:34,582
-( CLANKING )
-( FOOTSTEPS )

177
00:08:34,665 --> 00:08:36,375
I have to go.

178
00:08:36,458 --> 00:08:38,627
I'll find you before we start the riot.

179
00:08:41,589 --> 00:08:43,841
Hey, you! The warden wants to see you!

180
00:08:43,924 --> 00:08:44,967
Why?

181
00:08:45,050 --> 00:08:46,844
I don't know. I didn't ask.

182
00:08:46,927 --> 00:08:49,013
Maybe I could schedule
another time with him?

183
00:08:49,096 --> 00:08:50,222
How's tomorrow?

184
00:08:50,306 --> 00:08:52,516
He wants to see you now.

185
00:08:56,270 --> 00:08:57,855
WARDEN: Put him in the lineup.

186
00:09:00,608 --> 00:09:02,735
( WHIMPERS )

187
00:09:03,736 --> 00:09:05,321
WARDEN: One of you is an imposter

188
00:09:05,404 --> 00:09:08,157
who thought he could fool me.

189
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:13,120
But now that person is going
to be in a lot of trouble.

190
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:15,915
Who is it?

191
00:09:17,041 --> 00:09:19,043
( TEETH CHATTERING )

192
00:09:22,254 --> 00:09:24,882
CHIT SANG: That's him, Warden.
He's the imposter!

193
00:09:25,966 --> 00:09:27,051
What?

194
00:09:29,261 --> 00:09:30,679
I am not!

195
00:09:30,763 --> 00:09:33,307
He's lying! He's a liar!

196
00:09:33,390 --> 00:09:34,683
( FOOTSTEPS )

197
00:09:36,894 --> 00:09:38,062
( EXHALES )

198
00:09:40,856 --> 00:09:45,653
- I'm telling you, it wasn't me.
- Save your breath.

199
00:09:45,736 --> 00:09:47,488
I know you've been working together.

200
00:09:47,571 --> 00:09:50,616
You threw Chit Sang in the very
cooler they used to escape.

201
00:09:50,699 --> 00:09:52,785
It was all part of your plan.

202
00:09:52,868 --> 00:09:54,912
That was just a coincidence!

203
00:09:54,995 --> 00:09:56,038
( DOOR OPENS )

204
00:09:56,121 --> 00:09:57,581
Sir, there's someone to see you.

205
00:09:57,706 --> 00:09:59,625
Who told you to interrupt me?

206
00:10:01,001 --> 00:10:02,544
I did.

207
00:10:03,712 --> 00:10:05,255
WARDEN: Princess Azula!

208
00:10:05,339 --> 00:10:07,758
Uh, it is an honor to welcome you

209
00:10:07,841 --> 00:10:10,344
to the Fire Nation's
most exemplary prison.

210
00:10:10,427 --> 00:10:12,388
I didn't realize you were coming.

211
00:10:12,554 --> 00:10:14,014
Who is this?

212
00:10:14,723 --> 00:10:15,933
He's a guard

213
00:10:16,016 --> 00:10:18,519
who was involved in a recent
and feeble escape attempt.

214
00:10:18,602 --> 00:10:21,605
- It wasn't me!
- Quiet, you!

215
00:10:21,689 --> 00:10:24,024
You're wasting your time.
That's not one of them.

216
00:10:25,234 --> 00:10:27,903
- How do you know?
- Because I'm a people person.

217
00:10:29,238 --> 00:10:30,614
( CLANK )

218
00:10:30,698 --> 00:10:32,449
( FOOTSTEPS )

219
00:10:34,159 --> 00:10:35,577
Hey, I just got orders.

220
00:10:35,661 --> 00:10:37,329
Let the prisoners out into the yard.

221
00:10:37,413 --> 00:10:39,164
But we're in the middle of lockdown.

222
00:10:39,289 --> 00:10:40,457
Oh, okay.

223
00:10:40,582 --> 00:10:42,334
I'll just go tell the
warden you said that.

224
00:10:42,626 --> 00:10:43,877
I'm sure he'll be glad

225
00:10:43,961 --> 00:10:45,838
to hear about you
undermining his authority.

226
00:10:45,921 --> 00:10:47,381
What's your name again?

227
00:10:47,506 --> 00:10:49,675
Wait, uh, don't tell the warden.

228
00:10:49,758 --> 00:10:51,176
I'm just a little confused.

229
00:10:51,301 --> 00:10:53,137
Hey, I'm confused, too.

230
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:55,931
But the warden's in a
bad mood and irrational.

231
00:10:56,056 --> 00:10:57,558
So if you ask me,

232
00:10:57,683 --> 00:11:00,686
it's best not to question it
and just do what he says.

233
00:11:01,145 --> 00:11:02,938
Yeah, you're right.

234
00:11:03,313 --> 00:11:05,524
- We're letting them out!
-( BELL RINGING )

235
00:11:18,787 --> 00:11:20,831
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

236
00:11:22,916 --> 00:11:25,377
This is it. We have to start a riot.

237
00:11:25,461 --> 00:11:27,337
Okay, but how do we do that?

238
00:11:27,421 --> 00:11:29,214
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

239
00:11:32,259 --> 00:11:33,260
I'll show you.

240
00:11:35,763 --> 00:11:36,764
( GRUNTS )

241
00:11:36,847 --> 00:11:39,016
Hey! What did you do that for?

242
00:11:39,099 --> 00:11:40,476
That hurt my feelings.

243
00:11:40,559 --> 00:11:41,977
Aren't you mad at me?

244
00:11:42,061 --> 00:11:44,188
Uh, well, normally I would be,

245
00:11:44,271 --> 00:11:46,774
but I've been learning
to control my anger.

246
00:11:46,857 --> 00:11:47,900
( SQUEAKING )

247
00:11:47,983 --> 00:11:49,234
This isn't working.

248
00:11:49,318 --> 00:11:50,527
Hey, you!

249
00:11:50,611 --> 00:11:52,613
You're lucky I didn't rat you out.

250
00:11:52,696 --> 00:11:54,823
But my generosity comes with a price.

251
00:11:55,115 --> 00:11:58,702
I know you're planning another
escape attempt, and I want in.

252
00:11:59,078 --> 00:12:01,497
Actually, we're trying
to escape right now,

253
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:02,998
but we need a riot.

254
00:12:03,082 --> 00:12:05,959
You wouldn't happen to know
how to start one, would you?

255
00:12:06,043 --> 00:12:08,337
A prison riot? Please.

256
00:12:08,962 --> 00:12:10,380
( GASPS )

257
00:12:12,549 --> 00:12:15,344
Hey! Riot!

258
00:12:15,552 --> 00:12:17,554
( PRISONERS SHOUTING )

259
00:12:20,432 --> 00:12:21,767
Impressive.

260
00:12:23,143 --> 00:12:24,770
Forget about controlling my anger.

261
00:12:24,853 --> 00:12:26,355
Let's riot! Whoa!

262
00:12:27,606 --> 00:12:28,649
( GRUNTS )

263
00:12:29,608 --> 00:12:31,235
( SHOOTING )

264
00:12:31,318 --> 00:12:33,070
( GRUNTING )

265
00:12:33,737 --> 00:12:35,697
WARDEN: Who let these
prisoners into the yard?

266
00:12:35,781 --> 00:12:38,033
This is supposed to be a lockdown!

267
00:12:39,368 --> 00:12:40,452
( SQUEAK )

268
00:12:40,536 --> 00:12:41,912
( TWINKLING )

269
00:12:43,288 --> 00:12:44,540
Ma'am, there's a riot going on.

270
00:12:44,623 --> 00:12:45,707
I'm here to protect you.

271
00:12:45,791 --> 00:12:49,670
- I don't need any protection.
- Heh, believe me, she doesn't.

272
00:12:49,753 --> 00:12:51,964
I'm sorry, but I'm under
direct orders from your uncle

273
00:12:52,047 --> 00:12:53,382
to make sure nothing happens.

274
00:12:53,465 --> 00:12:54,925
( FIRE RUMBLING )

275
00:12:55,217 --> 00:12:56,552
Get off of me!

276
00:13:04,268 --> 00:13:05,894
( SHOUTING )

277
00:13:05,978 --> 00:13:07,563
( SHOOTING )

278
00:13:11,441 --> 00:13:13,277
Zuko, good. We're all here.

279
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,611
Now, all we need to do

280
00:13:14,695 --> 00:13:16,822
is grab the warden
and get to the gondolas.

281
00:13:16,905 --> 00:13:17,990
And how do we do that?

282
00:13:18,991 --> 00:13:20,450
I'm not sure.

283
00:13:20,534 --> 00:13:23,036
Ugh, I thought you'd thought this through!

284
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:24,204
I thought you told me

285
00:13:24,288 --> 00:13:26,039
it's okay not to think everything through!

286
00:13:26,123 --> 00:13:29,334
Maybe not everything,
but this is kind of important.

287
00:13:30,294 --> 00:13:31,670
CHIT SANG: Hey, uh, fellas?

288
00:13:31,753 --> 00:13:33,589
I think your girlfriend's
taking care of it.

289
00:13:33,672 --> 00:13:35,632
( PRISONERS SHOUTING )

290
00:13:35,716 --> 00:13:37,134
( SHOOTING )

291
00:13:37,217 --> 00:13:39,219
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

292
00:13:40,429 --> 00:13:42,389
♪

293
00:13:48,061 --> 00:13:49,104
( GRUNTS )

294
00:13:49,188 --> 00:13:50,731
♪

295
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:04,995
You wouldn't dare.

296
00:14:06,413 --> 00:14:07,581
( GRUNTS )

297
00:14:08,457 --> 00:14:11,376
Sorry, Warden. You're my prisoner now.

298
00:14:11,752 --> 00:14:13,045
( GRUNTS )

299
00:14:13,128 --> 00:14:15,339
We've got the warden.
Now let's get out of here.

300
00:14:15,422 --> 00:14:16,465
( PANTING )

301
00:14:16,548 --> 00:14:19,218
- That's some girl.
- Tell me about it.

302
00:14:29,019 --> 00:14:30,312
We're almost there.

303
00:14:33,607 --> 00:14:34,691
( GRUNTS )

304
00:14:34,775 --> 00:14:36,443
( FIRE RUMBLING )

305
00:14:37,486 --> 00:14:39,571
Back off! We've got the warden.

306
00:14:41,406 --> 00:14:42,449
( GRUNTS )

307
00:14:44,910 --> 00:14:46,119
Let's go.

308
00:14:46,203 --> 00:14:48,205
( TENSE MUSIC )

309
00:14:48,664 --> 00:14:51,667
♪

310
00:14:56,838 --> 00:14:57,923
Everyone in.

311
00:14:58,006 --> 00:15:00,008
♪

312
00:15:03,428 --> 00:15:04,888
( CLICKING )

313
00:15:04,972 --> 00:15:06,974
( CREAKING )

314
00:15:08,475 --> 00:15:10,435
( WHIRRING )

315
00:15:12,562 --> 00:15:14,731
( GRUNTS )

316
00:15:21,405 --> 00:15:22,948
( SHOOTING )

317
00:15:24,866 --> 00:15:26,952
( GROANS )

318
00:15:29,329 --> 00:15:30,622
What are you doing?

319
00:15:30,706 --> 00:15:32,874
I'm making it so they can't stop us.

320
00:15:32,958 --> 00:15:34,251
Way to think ahead.

321
00:15:34,334 --> 00:15:37,379
- SUKI: We're on our way.
- Wait, who's that?

322
00:15:38,797 --> 00:15:40,173
ZUKO: That's a problem.

323
00:15:40,257 --> 00:15:41,967
It's my sister and her friend.

324
00:15:42,050 --> 00:15:43,969
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

325
00:15:45,387 --> 00:15:47,389
♪

326
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:56,815
( WHOOSH )

327
00:15:56,898 --> 00:15:58,900
♪

328
00:16:05,157 --> 00:16:07,784
This is a rematch I've been waiting for.

329
00:16:07,868 --> 00:16:08,869
Me too.

330
00:16:08,952 --> 00:16:10,704
♪

331
00:16:32,809 --> 00:16:35,270
( WHOOSHING )

332
00:16:39,399 --> 00:16:41,401
( GRUNTING )

333
00:16:47,699 --> 00:16:49,117
( GRUNTS )

334
00:16:50,035 --> 00:16:52,079
♪

335
00:16:57,042 --> 00:16:59,211
( WHOOSHING )

336
00:16:59,294 --> 00:17:01,463
♪

337
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:17,062
( WARDEN GRUNTS )

338
00:17:17,145 --> 00:17:18,397
MALE GUARD: There's the warden.

339
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,481
I see him!

340
00:17:20,399 --> 00:17:21,608
( WARDEN GRUNTS )

341
00:17:22,984 --> 00:17:24,778
Cut the line!

342
00:17:24,861 --> 00:17:26,321
He wants us to cut the line.

343
00:17:26,405 --> 00:17:29,366
But if we cut the line,
there's no way he'll survive.

344
00:17:29,449 --> 00:17:30,826
He knows that.

345
00:17:30,909 --> 00:17:32,911
( CREAKING )

346
00:17:34,413 --> 00:17:36,039
( BLASTS )

347
00:17:36,123 --> 00:17:38,125
♪

348
00:17:42,295 --> 00:17:44,297
( CREAKING )

349
00:17:47,175 --> 00:17:49,010
( GROANS )

350
00:17:50,303 --> 00:17:51,805
( PANTS )

351
00:17:56,726 --> 00:17:58,603
They're about to cut the line!

352
00:17:58,687 --> 00:18:00,105
♪

353
00:18:06,445 --> 00:18:08,447
( WHIRRING )

354
00:18:09,823 --> 00:18:11,700
Then it's time to leave.

355
00:18:13,535 --> 00:18:14,703
( BLAST )

356
00:18:14,786 --> 00:18:16,204
Goodbye, Zuko.

357
00:18:16,288 --> 00:18:17,664
( EERIE MUSIC )

358
00:18:17,747 --> 00:18:19,499
♪

359
00:18:29,926 --> 00:18:32,554
They're cutting the line!
The gondola's about to go!

360
00:18:32,637 --> 00:18:34,389
CHIT SANG: I hope this thing floats.

361
00:18:34,473 --> 00:18:36,099
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

362
00:18:36,183 --> 00:18:38,185
♪

363
00:18:43,648 --> 00:18:45,775
( GRUNTING )

364
00:18:45,859 --> 00:18:47,319
What are you doing?

365
00:18:48,111 --> 00:18:49,905
Saving the jerk who dumped me.

366
00:18:52,407 --> 00:18:54,117
( FIRE RUMBLING )

367
00:18:59,831 --> 00:19:00,957
( GROANING )

368
00:19:03,376 --> 00:19:04,503
Whoa!

369
00:19:04,586 --> 00:19:05,879
( GRUNTING )

370
00:19:07,839 --> 00:19:08,882
( GRUNTING )

371
00:19:11,051 --> 00:19:12,511
( CREAKING )

372
00:19:16,181 --> 00:19:17,474
Who is that?

373
00:19:22,938 --> 00:19:24,105
It's Mai.

374
00:19:24,189 --> 00:19:26,650
What is she doing?

375
00:19:26,733 --> 00:19:28,193
( "I DON'T KNOW" SOUND )

376
00:19:30,695 --> 00:19:32,697
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

377
00:19:32,781 --> 00:19:34,783
♪

378
00:19:39,579 --> 00:19:41,581
( GRUNTS )

379
00:19:43,667 --> 00:19:45,043
Sorry, Warden.

380
00:19:45,126 --> 00:19:47,546
Your record is officially broken.

381
00:19:48,129 --> 00:19:50,423
( GRUNTS )

382
00:19:51,007 --> 00:19:52,050
( PANTING )

383
00:19:52,133 --> 00:19:54,302
Well, we made it out. Now what?

384
00:19:56,596 --> 00:19:59,891
- Zuko, what are you doing?
- My sister was on that island.

385
00:19:59,975 --> 00:20:03,478
Yeah, and she's probably right
behind us, so let's not stop.

386
00:20:03,562 --> 00:20:05,564
What I mean is she must've
come here somehow.

387
00:20:07,857 --> 00:20:10,151
There! That's our way out of here.

388
00:20:10,235 --> 00:20:12,237
♪

389
00:20:19,369 --> 00:20:20,787
AZUKA: Leave us alone.

390
00:20:25,584 --> 00:20:27,627
I never expected this from you.

391
00:20:31,631 --> 00:20:33,967
The thing I don't understand is why.

392
00:20:34,050 --> 00:20:37,637
Why would you do it?
You know the consequences.

393
00:20:39,806 --> 00:20:41,391
I guess you just don't know people

394
00:20:41,474 --> 00:20:43,226
as well as you think you do.

395
00:20:43,310 --> 00:20:45,020
You miscalculated.

396
00:20:45,103 --> 00:20:47,689
I love Zuko more than I fear you.

397
00:20:48,356 --> 00:20:51,484
No, you miscalculated!
You should've feared me more!

398
00:20:55,447 --> 00:20:56,948
( GRUNTS )

399
00:20:59,451 --> 00:21:01,202
( GASPS )

400
00:21:03,163 --> 00:21:05,582
Come on! Let's get outta here!

401
00:21:09,669 --> 00:21:11,338
You're both fools!

402
00:21:13,632 --> 00:21:15,842
What shall we do with them, Princess?

403
00:21:15,925 --> 00:21:17,093
AZUKA: Put them somewhere

404
00:21:17,177 --> 00:21:20,889
I'll never have to see their
faces again, and let them rot!

405
00:21:21,556 --> 00:21:23,558
( CRICKETS CHIRPING )

406
00:21:29,147 --> 00:21:30,857
KATARA: What are you doing in this thing?

407
00:21:30,940 --> 00:21:32,442
What happened to the war balloon?

408
00:21:32,525 --> 00:21:33,777
It kinda got destroyed.

409
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:36,237
Sounds like a crazy fishing trip.

410
00:21:36,321 --> 00:21:38,198
Did you at least get some good meat?

411
00:21:38,281 --> 00:21:41,159
I did, the best meat of all.

412
00:21:41,242 --> 00:21:44,037
The meat of friendship and fatherhood.

413
00:21:47,832 --> 00:21:50,126
I'm new. What's up, everybody?

414
00:21:50,210 --> 00:21:51,419
Dad.

415
00:21:52,462 --> 00:21:53,838
Hi, Katara.

416
00:21:58,551 --> 00:22:00,220
How are you here?

417
00:22:00,303 --> 00:22:02,764
What is going on? Where did you go?

418
00:22:02,847 --> 00:22:05,809
We kind of went to a Fire Nation prison.

419
00:22:05,892 --> 00:22:07,602
♪

420
00:22:10,814 --> 00:22:13,775
TOPH: Seriously,
you guys didn't find any meat?

421
00:22:13,858 --> 00:22:16,861
♪

422
00:22:28,498 --> 00:22:31,501
( MALE VOCALIZING DRUMBEATS )

423
00:22:40,135 --> 00:22:42,137
♪

424
00:22:54,899 --> 00:22:56,901
♪
